        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): make the sidebar resizable",
        "body": "Closes #102453\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Control UI sidebar has a fixed width, so long session names and navigation labels truncate even when the browser has ample horizontal space.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds an accessible desktop resize handle using the existing divider component, clamps the sidebar to 240–400 px, and persists the selected width. Collapsed, onboarding, and mobile drawer layouts keep their existing fixed behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can drag the sidebar edge or use keyboard controls to make navigation narrower or wider. The chosen width survives reloads.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox: 28 settings tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox: 2 Control UI browser E2E scenarios passed, covering pointer drag, persistence, viewport resize, Home/End keyboard limits, collapsed rail, and mobile drawer behavior.\n- Blacksmith Testbox: `pnpm check:changed` passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox: `pnpm build` passed, including the production Control UI build.\n- Fresh autoreview: no actionable findings (0.94 confidence).\n- Synthetic before/after screenshots will be attached to the PR; no user data is included.\n\nAI-assisted implementation; maintainer-reviewed and verified with the commands above.\n",
